On Tuesday, November 20, 2012 2:57:04 PM UTC-5, Bob Carpenter wrote:<div> </div><blockquote class="gmail_quote" style="margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex">What I was thinking from Ben&#39;s suggestion was something
<br>like this:
<br>
<br>parameters {
<br>   simplex[K] theta;
<br>   ...
<br>transformed parameters {
<br>   vector[K-1] cutpoints;
<br>   real sum;
<br>   sum &lt;- 0.0;
<br>   for (k in 1:(K-1)) {
<br>     sum &lt;- sum + theta[k];
<br>     cutpoints[k] &lt;- inv_logit[sum];
<br>   }
<br>   ...
<br></blockquote>
